{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}19x+3y-4z=-2 \\\\ 6x+ky-4z=-1 \\\\ -9x-y+2z=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $y=21$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $2k+20,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-42684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}19 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 6 & k & -4 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2k+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}19 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =19\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =19(-2+20)+2(12-36)-4(30-9) \\\\  & =342-48-84 \\\\  & =210.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{210}{2k+20}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=21.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{210}{2k+20} & =21 \\\\ 10 & =2k+20 \\\\ 2k & =-10 \\\\ k & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-42684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44711afdfe793b35e9c3be72d0a6429a9657ecb1442d32e26d4ae8ad74b859ce"} {"question" "q-42684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-42684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-2"] ["math" "k=-5"] ["math" "k=-6"] ["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-42684" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z=2 \\\\ x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-1,$ then $x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+1z=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z=2 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-1)z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3-4)-2(-2-4)+(2-3) \\\\  & =-7+12-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{4}{-1}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44711afdfe793b35e9c3be72d0a6429a9657ecb1442d32e26d4ae8ad74b859ce"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-43108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+5z=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y+2z=0 \\\\ x+4y=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $x=-4$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $15,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ k & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ k & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-8)+(0-2k)+5(0-3k) \\\\  & =8-2k-15k \\\\  & =8-17k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{8-17k}{15}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=-4.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8-17k}{15} & =-4 \\\\ 8-17k & =-60 \\\\ -17k & =-68 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44711afdfe793b35e9c3be72d0a6429a9657ecb1442d32e26d4ae8ad74b859ce"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-2"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-4"] ["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-73697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y-2z=-7 \\\\ 2x+y-4z=-10 \\\\ 3x-3y-2z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $16,$ then $z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-5)y+(-2z)=-7 \\\\ 2x+1y+(-4)z=-10 \\\\ 3x+(-3)y+(-2)z=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{aligned}|-(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-7-30)+5(-14+30)-7(-6-3) \\\\  & =-111+80+63 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{32}{16}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44711afdfe793b35e9c3be72d0a6429a9657ecb1442d32e26d4ae8ad74b859ce"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-14"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-139989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y-5z=1 \\\\ 2x+3y-3z=k \\\\ -5x+3y+7z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-19,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}|+(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(7k-6)-(14-15)-5(-4+5k) \\\\  & =21k-18+1+20-25k \\\\  & =-4k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-4k+3}{-19}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4k+3}{-19} & =-1 \\\\ -4k+3 & =19 \\\\ -4k & =16 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44711afdfe793b35e9c3be72d0a6429a9657ecb1442d32e26d4ae8ad74b859ce"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-4"] ["math" "k=0"] ["math" "k=2"] ["math" "k=7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063726/state.json" "file_sha256" "3242291ab540ec7ca0a5649f091041c2eb2cded3996b427014fea063217778fc"} {"question" "q-140042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer